WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.385 --> 00:00:02.726
- He was an American self-help author

00:00:02.726 --> 00:00:04.272
and motivational speaker.

00:00:04.272 --> 00:00:06.053
His first book, The Erroneous Zone,

00:00:06.053 --> 00:00:08.398
is one of the best-selling
books of all time,

00:00:08.398 --> 00:00:12.169
with over 35 million
copies sold worldwide.

00:00:12.169 --> 00:00:13.870
He spent most of his early life,

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:15.598
up until the age of ten,

00:00:15.598 --> 00:00:17.873
in an orphanage on the
East Side of Detroit,

00:00:17.873 --> 00:00:20.462
after his father walked out on his family.

00:00:20.462 --> 00:00:21.859
He's Wayne Dyer and here are

00:00:21.859 --> 00:00:24.022
his top ten rules for success.

00:00:24.022 --> 00:00:26.439
(explosion)

00:00:27.561 --> 00:00:29.311
- You can't give away

00:00:30.361 --> 00:00:32.028
what you don't have.

00:00:32.991 --> 00:00:34.882
Now it sounds ridiculous, okay?

00:00:34.882 --> 00:00:39.049
But it's more than what meets
the ear as you hear this,

00:00:39.952 --> 00:00:43.110
you can't give away what you don't have.

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:47.385
People who are not good
at giving away love,

00:00:47.385 --> 00:00:49.640
can't give away love

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:52.810
because they don't have it to give away.

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:55.879
If I want to give you a dozen oranges,

00:00:55.879 --> 00:00:58.130
I can't give you those dozen oranges

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:02.609
unless I go out and pick
up 12 oranges someplace.

00:01:02.609 --> 00:01:06.870
Otherwise all it is is
just empty rhetoric,

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:08.155
and the same thing is true of

00:01:08.155 --> 00:01:10.213
virtually everything in your life.

00:01:10.213 --> 00:01:13.326
You can't give away love for others,

00:01:13.326 --> 00:01:16.601
if you don't have love
in here to give away.

00:01:16.601 --> 00:01:19.194
If what you have in here is contempt,

00:01:19.194 --> 00:01:21.208
if what you have in here is anger,

00:01:21.208 --> 00:01:23.279
if what you have in here is fear,

00:01:23.279 --> 00:01:24.871
then these are the things you're going

00:01:24.871 --> 00:01:27.425
to be giving away in your life.

00:01:27.425 --> 00:01:29.263
The second thing that the
ego teaches us is that

00:01:29.263 --> 00:01:32.142
who I am is not only what I have,

00:01:32.142 --> 00:01:36.004
but who I am is what I
do, what I accomplish.

00:01:36.004 --> 00:01:39.052
And so we spend a big hunk of our lives,

00:01:39.052 --> 00:01:43.069
believing that the way that
we become quote successful,

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:45.066
happy, fulfilled, self-extolized,

00:01:45.066 --> 00:01:46.533
whatever it might be,

00:01:46.533 --> 00:01:50.098
is on the basis of what I accomplish,

00:01:50.098 --> 00:01:52.265
what my resume looks like,

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.729
how many promotions I get,

00:01:55.729 --> 00:01:59.428
and so we send our children off to school,

00:01:59.428 --> 00:02:02.252
and we ask them to learn,

00:02:02.252 --> 00:02:06.329
to identify themselves
on how much they get

00:02:06.329 --> 00:02:07.885
and what they accomplish.

00:02:07.885 --> 00:02:09.880
Your grades become more important

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:12.537
than what it is that you are studying.

00:02:12.537 --> 00:02:14.932
What you own, what clothes you wear,

00:02:14.932 --> 00:02:17.435
what labels you have, and so on,

00:02:17.435 --> 00:02:20.680
and we become obsessed with
this kind of absurdity,

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:23.650
and this is the false self at work.

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:25.413
There are many ways to get the things

00:02:25.413 --> 00:02:27.816
that we want for ourselves in our lives,

00:02:27.816 --> 00:02:30.483
but basically it all begins with

00:02:31.423 --> 00:02:33.900
how we choose to think.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:34.983
As you think,

00:02:36.175 --> 00:02:38.079
so shall you be.

00:02:38.079 --> 00:02:40.699
Seven little words that
I think are perhaps

00:02:40.699 --> 00:02:42.806
the most important things that we can

00:02:42.806 --> 00:02:45.632
learn and master in our lives.

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:48.286
This old proverb notion

00:02:48.286 --> 00:02:51.872
that I become what I
think about all day long,

00:02:51.872 --> 00:02:55.582
and once you know that
what you think about

00:02:55.582 --> 00:02:57.729
is what expands,

00:02:57.729 --> 00:03:01.808
you start getting real careful
about what you think about.

00:03:01.808 --> 00:03:03.130
You don't allow your thoughts to be on

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:05.317
anything that you don't want,

00:03:05.317 --> 00:03:06.885
or that you wouldn't want to have manifest

00:03:06.885 --> 00:03:08.901
or show up for you in your life.

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:12.068
Have a mind that is open to everything

00:03:13.917 --> 00:03:15.917
and attached to nothing.

00:03:17.123 --> 00:03:19.182
One of the central principles of my life

00:03:19.182 --> 00:03:21.432
is that no-one knows enough

00:03:22.386 --> 00:03:25.886
to be a pessimist about anything,

00:03:25.886 --> 00:03:28.739
and that each and every one of us,

00:03:28.739 --> 00:03:33.480
when we close our mind to
what is possible for us,

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:36.118
or what is possible for humanity,

00:03:36.118 --> 00:03:37.868
closes off the genius

00:03:39.884 --> 00:03:44.318
that resides and lives in
each and every one of us.

00:03:44.318 --> 00:03:48.323
Having an open mind
doesn't necessarily mean

00:03:48.323 --> 00:03:50.382
finding fault with all of the things

00:03:50.382 --> 00:03:52.236
that you have been taught by others.

00:03:52.236 --> 00:03:54.819
It means opening yourself up to

00:03:55.757 --> 00:03:58.300
the potentiality and the possibility

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:01.242
that anything and everything is possible,

00:04:01.242 --> 00:04:04.183
so having a mind that
is open to everything

00:04:04.183 --> 00:04:06.606
and attached to nothing,

00:04:06.606 --> 00:04:09.963
really means finding within ourselves

00:04:09.963 --> 00:04:12.490
the ability to get rid of a trait

00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:16.490
that I find so common in
the contemporary world.

00:04:18.452 --> 00:04:22.241
Do you know that most people that I meet

00:04:22.241 --> 00:04:23.658
spend their lives

00:04:24.527 --> 00:04:26.277
looking for occasions

00:04:28.535 --> 00:04:29.785
to be offended?

00:04:31.946 --> 00:04:34.869
They actually are out there hoping

00:04:34.869 --> 00:04:38.369
that they can find some
reason to be offended,

00:04:38.369 --> 00:04:40.278
and there's no shortage of reasons,

00:04:40.278 --> 00:04:41.835
they're out there everywhere.

00:04:41.835 --> 00:04:44.499
The way this person dressed,
what this person said,

00:04:44.499 --> 00:04:46.531
they turned on their
TV, they hear the news,

00:04:46.531 --> 00:04:48.006
they're offended by this,

00:04:48.006 --> 00:04:51.651
someone used language
that they didn't like,

00:04:51.651 --> 00:04:53.857
someone doesn't share the
same customs that you--

00:04:53.857 --> 00:04:55.142
and people all day long--

00:04:55.142 --> 00:04:57.634
in fact, if you keep track tomorrow,

00:04:57.634 --> 00:05:00.967
you will find probably a hundred reasons

00:05:02.665 --> 00:05:05.118
that you can go around being offended,

00:05:05.118 --> 00:05:06.849
but a mind that is open to everything

00:05:06.849 --> 00:05:09.864
and attached to nothing
is a mind that says,

00:05:09.864 --> 00:05:13.282
"I'm never looking for
anything to be offended by."

00:05:13.282 --> 00:05:15.913
And that whatever anybody
else out there has to say,

00:05:15.913 --> 00:05:18.491
my response to that is,

00:05:18.491 --> 00:05:20.736
"That's an interesting point of view."

00:05:20.736 --> 00:05:22.901
"I've never considered that before.

00:05:22.901 --> 00:05:26.484
When you change the
way you look at things,

00:05:28.578 --> 00:05:31.078
the things you look at change.

00:05:32.267 --> 00:05:34.697
Albert Einstein once observed that

00:05:34.697 --> 00:05:38.152
you have the most fundamental
and major decision

00:05:38.152 --> 00:05:41.735
that you have to make
in your life is this.

00:05:42.803 --> 00:05:44.720
Do I live in a friendly

00:05:46.545 --> 00:05:48.933
or a hostile universe?

00:05:48.933 --> 00:05:50.237
Which is it?

00:05:50.237 --> 00:05:53.262
Is it a universe that
is filled with hostility

00:05:53.262 --> 00:05:55.466
and anger and people
wanting to hate each other,

00:05:55.466 --> 00:05:57.139
and people wanting to kill each other,

00:05:57.139 --> 00:05:58.244
is that what you see?

00:05:58.244 --> 00:06:01.036
Because when you see the world that way,

00:06:01.036 --> 00:06:02.467
that's exactly what you will

00:06:02.467 --> 00:06:04.175
create for yourself in your life.

00:06:04.175 --> 00:06:06.334
This is from great scientific minds,

00:06:06.334 --> 00:06:08.052
and the interesting thing is that

00:06:08.052 --> 00:06:11.760
this is not just a clever play on words,

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:13.585
that when you change the
way you look at things,

00:06:13.585 --> 00:06:15.075
the things you look at change.

00:06:15.075 --> 00:06:17.645
It's actually a very scientific thing

00:06:17.645 --> 00:06:21.274
and I'm going to show you
that in just a moment.

00:06:21.274 --> 00:06:24.521
I'd like you to imagine
the following scene;

00:06:24.521 --> 00:06:26.271
you're in your house,

00:06:27.986 --> 00:06:31.162
you've got your car keys in your hand,

00:06:31.162 --> 00:06:33.912
the lights go out, power failure.

00:06:34.767 --> 00:06:36.659
You can't see a thing,

00:06:36.659 --> 00:06:39.278
you stumble around in your living room,

00:06:39.278 --> 00:06:41.994
and you drop your keys,

00:06:41.994 --> 00:06:43.346
and you look around for a moment,

00:06:43.346 --> 00:06:44.632
and you realize that you're never going

00:06:44.632 --> 00:06:46.448
to find them in the dark.

00:06:46.448 --> 00:06:48.635
But you look outside,

00:06:48.635 --> 00:06:51.175
and you notice that the
street lights are on,

00:06:51.175 --> 00:06:54.833
so in your mind a light bulb goes off.

00:06:54.833 --> 00:06:56.244
Hmm.

00:06:56.244 --> 00:06:57.727
I'm not going to sit
around here in the dark

00:06:57.727 --> 00:06:59.490
and grope around looking for my keys,

00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:01.055
when there's a light on outside,

00:07:01.055 --> 00:07:04.906
I'm going to go out here
under the street light,

00:07:04.906 --> 00:07:06.266
and I'm going to look for my keys.

00:07:06.266 --> 00:07:08.804
(audience laughter)

00:07:08.804 --> 00:07:09.637
Why are you laughing?

00:07:09.637 --> 00:07:11.512
This makes a lot of sense.

00:07:11.512 --> 00:07:13.591
So you're out here and
you're groping around,

00:07:13.591 --> 00:07:14.712
and you're looking for your keys,

00:07:14.712 --> 00:07:15.794
and you're looking and looking,

00:07:15.794 --> 00:07:16.930
and your neighbor comes along and says,

00:07:16.930 --> 00:07:18.160
"What happened, Wayne?"

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:20.266
"Well, I dropped my keys."

00:07:20.266 --> 00:07:22.832
"Well, I'll help you look for them."

00:07:22.832 --> 00:07:25.063
And the two of us are now down here

00:07:25.063 --> 00:07:26.601
looking for our keys,

00:07:26.601 --> 00:07:28.087
we're looking and finally he says to me,

00:07:28.087 --> 00:07:31.694
"Excuse me, but where
did you drop your keys?"

00:07:31.694 --> 00:07:34.473
"Well, I dropped them in the house."

00:07:34.473 --> 00:07:36.148
(audience laughter)

00:07:36.148 --> 00:07:38.281
He said, "You mean to tell me that you"

00:07:38.281 --> 00:07:41.194
"dropped your keys in the house,"

00:07:41.194 --> 00:07:42.773
"and you're looking for them
out here in the street?"

00:07:42.773 --> 00:07:43.890
"That doesn't make any sense."

00:07:43.890 --> 00:07:45.686
And I said, "Well, it
doesn't make any sense

00:07:45.686 --> 00:07:49.051
"to grope around in the dark
when there's light out here."

00:07:49.051 --> 00:07:50.969
Now you laugh, and you
think how silly that is,

00:07:50.969 --> 00:07:53.540
but isn't that exactly what we do

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:56.483
when we have a problem,
a difficulty, a struggle,

00:07:56.483 --> 00:07:59.192
that is located inside,

00:07:59.192 --> 00:08:02.959
and we're looking for
the solution outside?

00:08:02.959 --> 00:08:05.229
Someplace outside of ourselves.

00:08:05.229 --> 00:08:06.860
It would be like going to the doctor

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:09.035
and telling him all of your symptoms,

00:08:09.035 --> 00:08:09.908
and the doctor says,

00:08:09.908 --> 00:08:11.882
"Oh boy, you've got a lot of symptoms."

00:08:11.882 --> 00:08:14.272
And he starts writing out prescriptions.

00:08:14.272 --> 00:08:15.712
"You need a prescription
for this symptom,"

00:08:15.712 --> 00:08:17.444
"You need a prescription
for that symptom."

00:08:17.444 --> 00:08:19.467
And finally he gets this four or five,

00:08:19.467 --> 00:08:21.134
and you go to walk out, and you say,

00:08:21.134 --> 00:08:22.240
"Well, I'd like my prescriptions."

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:23.167
He says, "No, no, no."

00:08:23.167 --> 00:08:24.930
"I'll give this one to
your mother-in-law,"

00:08:24.930 --> 00:08:26.911
"And I'll give this one to your neighbor,"

00:08:26.911 --> 00:08:28.216
"And I'll give this one to your daughter,"

00:08:28.216 --> 00:08:30.849
"And I'll give this one to your father."

00:08:30.849 --> 00:08:33.883
I mean, you're the one with
the struggle, the difficulties,

00:08:33.883 --> 00:08:36.997
and expecting somebody else to change,

00:08:36.997 --> 00:08:39.958
or something outside of you to get better,

00:08:39.958 --> 00:08:42.639
in order for you to make your life work

00:08:42.639 --> 00:08:45.078
at this level that I'm calling intention,

00:08:45.078 --> 00:08:47.478
is something you have to
really take a hard look at.

00:08:47.478 --> 00:08:48.561
It's in here.

00:08:49.527 --> 00:08:52.667
I used to say that before I had children,

00:08:52.667 --> 00:08:55.888
I had eight theories about
how to raise children.

00:08:55.888 --> 00:08:57.778
(audience laughter)

00:08:57.778 --> 00:09:00.154
And now I have eight children,

00:09:00.154 --> 00:09:01.487
and no theories.

00:09:03.529 --> 00:09:06.497
But one of the things
I know about children,

00:09:06.497 --> 00:09:07.330
is that

00:09:09.164 --> 00:09:12.081
no-one likes being told what to do.

00:09:13.276 --> 00:09:16.488
And this isn't just
children, this is all of us.

00:09:16.488 --> 00:09:18.171
One of my favorite songs,

00:09:18.171 --> 00:09:21.807
it's a song from when I
was back in high school,

00:09:21.807 --> 00:09:24.855
♫ Oh give me land, lots of land

00:09:24.855 --> 00:09:28.511
♫ And the starry skies above

00:09:28.511 --> 00:09:30.677
♫ Don't fence me in

00:09:30.677 --> 00:09:32.707
Boy, you know it.
(audience laughter)

00:09:32.707 --> 00:09:34.520
Don't fence me in.

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:36.510
Don't restrict me.

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:38.760
Don't put boundaries on me,

00:09:39.667 --> 00:09:41.826
don't tell me what I can
do and what I can't do,

00:09:41.826 --> 00:09:43.032
don't tell me how to be there,

00:09:43.032 --> 00:09:44.733
don't tell me what to wear,

00:09:44.733 --> 00:09:46.163
what to think,

00:09:46.163 --> 00:09:48.468
don't tell me even how to do yoga,

00:09:48.468 --> 00:09:51.409
don't tell me, I don't want to be told.

00:09:51.409 --> 00:09:54.650
This is the soul speaking, always.

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:55.483
The soul

00:09:57.537 --> 00:09:59.204
is constantly having

00:10:00.536 --> 00:10:02.869
a desire to expand and grow,

00:10:05.717 --> 00:10:08.309
and anything or anyone
that comes into your life

00:10:08.309 --> 00:10:09.749
that attempts to do that,

00:10:09.749 --> 00:10:14.292
you will find yourself
fighting it and reaching back.

00:10:14.292 --> 00:10:17.209
There are no justified resentments.

00:10:18.779 --> 00:10:20.708
And this is a very difficult principle

00:10:20.708 --> 00:10:22.200
for many people to get,

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:25.533
but one that I believe very strongly in.

00:10:27.042 --> 00:10:29.904
I was in a group one time,

00:10:29.904 --> 00:10:32.487
of drug addicts and alcoholics,

00:10:36.121 --> 00:10:39.379
and I was one of the people that was

00:10:39.379 --> 00:10:42.278
a sponsor and leading this group,

00:10:42.278 --> 00:10:45.417
and the sign on the wall said,

00:10:45.417 --> 00:10:49.998
"There are no justified
resentments in this group."

00:10:49.998 --> 00:10:53.415
And what I said to that group that night,

00:10:54.937 --> 00:10:58.157
was, "No matter what
anybody says to you here,"

00:10:58.157 --> 00:11:02.324
"no matter what kind of anger
comes directed towards you,"

00:11:03.432 --> 00:11:06.789
"no matter how much
hate you may encounter"

00:11:06.789 --> 00:11:08.569
"showing up in your life,"

00:11:08.569 --> 00:11:11.652
"there are no justified resentments."

00:11:13.023 --> 00:11:17.396
Meaning that if you
carry around resentment

00:11:17.396 --> 00:11:21.086
inside of you about
anything or about anything,

00:11:21.086 --> 00:11:22.700
and I'm talking about the person

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:25.929
that you lent money to
and hasn't paid you back,

00:11:25.929 --> 00:11:28.447
I'm talking about the person in your life

00:11:28.447 --> 00:11:31.984
that you feel was abusive in your life,

00:11:31.984 --> 00:11:34.701
I'm talking about the
person who walked out on you

00:11:34.701 --> 00:11:37.273
and left you for somebody else,

00:11:37.273 --> 00:11:40.172
I'm talking about all of the things

00:11:40.172 --> 00:11:43.952
that you have justified in
your heart and in your life,

00:11:43.952 --> 00:11:48.144
that you have the right
to be resentful about,

00:11:48.144 --> 00:11:51.375
and I'm suggesting to you
that those resentments

00:11:51.375 --> 00:11:53.958
will always end up harming you,

00:11:55.133 --> 00:11:59.168
and creating in you a sense of despair.

00:11:59.168 --> 00:12:00.835
I've often said that

00:12:01.972 --> 00:12:04.889
no one ever dies from a snake bite.

00:12:05.851 --> 00:12:07.784
The snake bite will never kill you.

00:12:07.784 --> 00:12:09.384
You cannot be un-bitten,

00:12:09.384 --> 00:12:11.439
once you're bitten, you're bitten.

00:12:11.439 --> 00:12:14.189
But it's the venom that continues

00:12:15.162 --> 00:12:19.131
to pour through your
system after the bite,

00:12:19.131 --> 00:12:21.400
that will end up destroying you.

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:23.703
In my mind, as I think about this idea

00:12:23.703 --> 00:12:26.375
of getting what you really want,

00:12:26.375 --> 00:12:30.569
and being able to attract
it into your life,

00:12:30.569 --> 00:12:33.521
what we have to look at is basically

00:12:33.521 --> 00:12:37.688
the obstacles that we have
conditioned ourselves--

00:12:38.664 --> 00:12:41.683
and you notice I say that we
have conditioned ourselves,

00:12:41.683 --> 00:12:43.929
because I have never believed that we need

00:12:43.929 --> 00:12:46.019
to be putting the
responsibility on someone else.

00:12:46.019 --> 00:12:47.880
If you're conditioned it's because

00:12:47.880 --> 00:12:50.399
you have allowed yourself to become that.

00:12:50.399 --> 00:12:53.568
And if we conditioned ourselves to believe

00:12:53.568 --> 00:12:55.782
certain kinds of things,

00:12:55.782 --> 00:12:59.578
and one of the things that
we believe and hang on to,

00:12:59.578 --> 00:13:02.661
and live with is this whole idea that

00:13:03.881 --> 00:13:07.379
all of the things that
happened to me in my past

00:13:07.379 --> 00:13:09.179
are what are keeping me from doing

00:13:09.179 --> 00:13:10.998
what I'd like to do today.

00:13:10.998 --> 00:13:12.401
So we hang on to these things

00:13:12.401 --> 00:13:13.982
and we fill ourselves with blame,

00:13:13.982 --> 00:13:16.242
you say, "I'm the middle child."

00:13:16.242 --> 00:13:20.311
"I'm the youngest child,
I'm the oldest child."

00:13:20.311 --> 00:13:22.424
"I'm an only child."

00:13:22.424 --> 00:13:24.882
Any one of those is a great excuse,

00:13:24.882 --> 00:13:26.878
if you're the youngest child you can say,

00:13:26.878 --> 00:13:29.651
"Well how could I be making
decisions for myself"

00:13:29.651 --> 00:13:33.080
"and be a fully-functioning person today,"

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:34.375
"when I always had
somebody else telling me"

00:13:34.375 --> 00:13:35.581
"what to do my whole life?"

00:13:35.581 --> 00:13:37.074
"How could I think for myself?"

00:13:37.074 --> 00:13:40.392
If you're the oldest child you
can simply say to yourself,

00:13:40.392 --> 00:13:42.481
"Well, how could I be
expected to think for myself,"

00:13:42.481 --> 00:13:44.092
"I always had to think for somebody else,"

00:13:44.092 --> 00:13:46.146
"I was always doing it for somebody else."

00:13:46.146 --> 00:13:48.152
And that leave the middle child,

00:13:48.152 --> 00:13:51.262
the classic identity crisis, oh poor me.

00:13:51.262 --> 00:13:52.701
"My mother didn't even know my name."

00:13:52.701 --> 00:13:54.024
(audience laughter)

00:13:54.024 --> 00:13:55.518
"She was always calling
me by this one's name,"

00:13:55.518 --> 00:13:57.399
"or that one's name."
(audience laughter)

00:13:57.399 --> 00:13:59.261
"So I don't know where I fit in."

00:13:59.261 --> 00:14:02.105
So that takes care of everybody
except the only child,

00:14:02.105 --> 00:14:04.787
and of course the only child--

00:14:04.787 --> 00:14:05.620
Hmm, well.

00:14:06.774 --> 00:14:08.645
Your parents looked at you and said,

00:14:08.645 --> 00:14:09.810
"We won't be doing that again."

00:14:09.810 --> 00:14:11.483
Right?
(audience laughter)

00:14:11.483 --> 00:14:13.986
You have to live with
that, I don't, alright?

00:14:13.986 --> 00:14:15.777
So everybody, with their birth order,

00:14:15.777 --> 00:14:17.677
or with their mother
liked their sister better,

00:14:17.677 --> 00:14:19.625
or that we had enough,
or we didn't have enough,

00:14:19.625 --> 00:14:21.753
or we had too much, or
we lived in the North,

00:14:21.753 --> 00:14:23.407
we lived in the South, I'm too tall,

00:14:23.407 --> 00:14:25.539
I'm too short, I've got too much hair,

00:14:25.539 --> 00:14:27.439
I don't have enough hair.
(audience laughter)

00:14:27.439 --> 00:14:28.913
It's falling out, it's not falling out,

00:14:28.913 --> 00:14:31.648
whatever it is, we all have these excuses,

00:14:31.648 --> 00:14:34.529
and I call all of these
things that we hang on to

00:14:34.529 --> 00:14:36.762
and use to keep ourselves from reaching

00:14:36.762 --> 00:14:39.765
these higher places in our lives,

00:14:39.765 --> 00:14:40.598
the wake.

00:14:41.545 --> 00:14:43.786
I call it the wake.

00:14:43.786 --> 00:14:44.786
And the wake

00:14:47.045 --> 00:14:49.602
comes from a story that I
heard Alan Watts tell one time,

00:14:49.602 --> 00:14:52.283
and it was a very powerful story.

00:14:52.283 --> 00:14:55.504
He said your life is like a boat,

00:14:55.504 --> 00:15:00.355
and it's heading up the river
at, say 40 knots, alright?

00:15:00.355 --> 00:15:01.855
And as it's going,

00:15:02.874 --> 00:15:07.041
you are somehow able to
metaphorically stand on the stern,

00:15:07.041 --> 00:15:09.703
the back of the boat, and
look down into the water.

00:15:09.703 --> 00:15:11.464
Now there goes your
life in this direction,

00:15:11.464 --> 00:15:12.555
and you're standing here and you're

00:15:12.555 --> 00:15:14.022
looking down into the water,

00:15:14.022 --> 00:15:16.172
and you ask yourself
these three questions:

00:15:16.172 --> 00:15:17.884
The first question,

00:15:17.884 --> 00:15:19.402
what is the wake?

00:15:19.402 --> 00:15:22.391
What is it, what is
this thing that you see?

00:15:22.391 --> 00:15:24.038
And the answer?

00:15:24.038 --> 00:15:27.538
The wake is the trail that is left behind.

00:15:29.229 --> 00:15:30.605
That's what it is.

00:15:30.605 --> 00:15:32.444
Nothing more, nothing less,

00:15:32.444 --> 00:15:34.411
it's the trail that is left behind.

00:15:34.411 --> 00:15:37.443
Second question to ask yourself
in this little metaphor,

00:15:37.443 --> 00:15:39.334
what's driving the boat?

00:15:39.334 --> 00:15:42.233
What's making this thing
go in this direction?

00:15:42.233 --> 00:15:43.744
The answer?

00:15:43.744 --> 00:15:46.542
The present moment energy

00:15:46.542 --> 00:15:50.025
that's being generated by the engine,

00:15:50.025 --> 00:15:51.283
and nothing more.

00:15:51.283 --> 00:15:52.913
That's the only thing that's making

00:15:52.913 --> 00:15:55.468
the boat go in this direction,

00:15:55.468 --> 00:15:57.476
and in this little scene,

00:15:57.476 --> 00:16:01.643
this means it's the present
moment thoughts that I have

00:16:02.747 --> 00:16:05.222
and how I am using them that is making

00:16:05.222 --> 00:16:07.995
my life go in this
direction, and nothing more.

00:16:07.995 --> 00:16:09.172
Because the third question is

00:16:09.172 --> 00:16:11.530
the most important and powerful question.

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:13.097
And ever since I heard it,

00:16:13.097 --> 00:16:14.590
I've always thought about
this whenever I have

00:16:14.590 --> 00:16:18.673
a tendency to look back
here and blame something.

00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:23.843
Is it possible for the
wake to drive the boat?

00:16:26.628 --> 00:16:29.843
That is, can a trail that is left behind

00:16:29.843 --> 00:16:33.105
make a boat go in this direction?

00:16:33.105 --> 00:16:36.124
And of course the answer to that is no.

00:16:36.124 --> 00:16:38.668
It can't, it's just a
trail that is left behind,

00:16:38.668 --> 00:16:41.995
and in that trail there are
an enormous number of things,

00:16:41.995 --> 00:16:44.285
and every one of us has a wake.

00:16:44.285 --> 00:16:45.940
And we have a whole lot of stuff in it,

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:49.214
and one of the problems that we have,

00:16:49.214 --> 00:16:52.265
is that we have a tendency to

00:16:52.265 --> 00:16:55.351
look at the wake and all
of the stuff that's in it,

00:16:55.351 --> 00:16:58.393
to explain why it is my life isn't working

00:16:58.393 --> 00:16:59.831
the way I would like it to work.

00:16:59.831 --> 00:17:02.630
So this was something that Portia Nelson,

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:05.655
who I knew, who passed
away a few years back,

00:17:05.655 --> 00:17:08.237
ten years back now, she
lived up in Seattle,

00:17:08.237 --> 00:17:11.904
and she was at a seminar
and they were asked

00:17:13.042 --> 00:17:16.375
to write the autobiography of their life

00:17:18.196 --> 00:17:20.696
in five verses, five chapters.

00:17:22.902 --> 00:17:25.757
And they gave them only cards this size,

00:17:25.757 --> 00:17:27.459
actually they were smaller than this.

00:17:27.459 --> 00:17:29.204
They were 3x5 cards,

00:17:29.204 --> 00:17:30.952
so write out Chapter One of your life,

00:17:30.952 --> 00:17:33.244
and just go to where you are today.

00:17:33.244 --> 00:17:35.860
And I remember doing this very same thing,

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:38.003
but what she wrote was so brilliant,

00:17:38.003 --> 00:17:41.086
that I asked her daughter if we could

00:17:42.115 --> 00:17:44.346
put it on public television, which I did,

00:17:44.346 --> 00:17:45.731
on the most recent show,

00:17:45.731 --> 00:17:49.348
and we made a contribution
to Portia's work.

00:17:49.348 --> 00:17:51.300
So this is what she wrote down in

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:54.381
the Chapter Five of her life:

00:17:54.381 --> 00:17:55.899
Chapter One,

00:17:55.899 --> 00:17:58.653
she said I walk down the street,

00:17:58.653 --> 00:18:01.723
there's a deep hole in the sidewalk,

00:18:01.723 --> 00:18:02.556
I fall in,

00:18:03.836 --> 00:18:04.669
I'm lost,

00:18:06.725 --> 00:18:08.421
I'm helpless.

00:18:08.421 --> 00:18:10.696
It isn't my fault,

00:18:10.696 --> 00:18:14.655
and it takes forever to find a way out.

00:18:14.655 --> 00:18:16.439
Chapter Two of my life,

00:18:16.439 --> 00:18:17.840
I walk down the same street,

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:20.441
there's a deep hole in the sidewalk.

00:18:20.441 --> 00:18:23.788
I pretend I don't see it.
(audience laughter)

00:18:23.788 --> 00:18:26.253
I fall in again.
(audience laughter)

00:18:26.253 --> 00:18:29.017
I can't believe I'm in the same place.

00:18:29.017 --> 00:18:30.989
It isn't my fault.

00:18:30.989 --> 00:18:34.731
It still takes a long
time for me to get out.

00:18:34.731 --> 00:18:37.234
Chapter Three of my life,

00:18:37.234 --> 00:18:38.734
I walk down the same street,

00:18:38.734 --> 00:18:41.786
there's a deep hole in the
sidewalk, I see it there.

00:18:41.786 --> 00:18:43.119
I still fall in,

00:18:43.997 --> 00:18:45.080
it's a habit,

00:18:46.300 --> 00:18:48.020
but my eyes are open,

00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:49.605
I know where I am,

00:18:49.605 --> 00:18:51.286
and it is my own fault,

00:18:51.286 --> 00:18:54.212
and I get out immediately.

00:18:54.212 --> 00:18:56.560
Chapter Four of my life,

00:18:56.560 --> 00:18:58.978
I walk down the same street,

00:18:58.978 --> 00:19:02.089
there's a deep hole in the sidewalk.

00:19:02.089 --> 00:19:03.506
I walk around it.

00:19:05.259 --> 00:19:07.259
Chapter Five of my life,

00:19:09.131 --> 00:19:12.048
finally I walk down another street.

00:19:14.278 --> 00:19:17.914
Isn't that great?
(laughter and applause)

00:19:17.914 --> 00:19:20.314
The next principle I call,

00:19:20.314 --> 00:19:23.564
don't die with your music still in you.

00:19:24.973 --> 00:19:26.986
And who better to quote than Theroux,

00:19:26.986 --> 00:19:28.887
right here in Concorde,

00:19:28.887 --> 00:19:33.608
When he talked about some of
us hear a different drummer?

00:19:33.608 --> 00:19:37.532
And we must march to
the music that we hear.

00:19:37.532 --> 00:19:39.718
But all of you, everybody watching,

00:19:39.718 --> 00:19:43.051
everybody here in this beautiful parish.

00:19:43.921 --> 00:19:46.727
All of you have some music playing,

00:19:46.727 --> 00:19:49.888
and all of you have a heroic mission.

00:19:49.888 --> 00:19:52.137
There's no accidents in this universe,

00:19:52.137 --> 00:19:55.054
we all show up here with a purpose.

00:19:56.131 --> 00:19:57.667
There's an intelligence that is

00:19:57.667 --> 00:19:59.336
a part of everything and everyone,

00:19:59.336 --> 00:20:01.882
and all of us are connected to it.

00:20:01.882 --> 00:20:03.382
And too many of us

00:20:05.705 --> 00:20:09.872
are afraid to listen to
that music and march to it.

00:20:11.636 --> 00:20:12.803
You out there,

00:20:14.561 --> 00:20:17.255
I know you have a book
you wanted to write.

00:20:17.255 --> 00:20:19.614
I know there's a composition
you wanted to compose,

00:20:19.614 --> 00:20:22.772
I know there's a song you
want to sing someplace.

00:20:22.772 --> 00:20:25.777
Maybe you want to raise
horses out in Montana,

00:20:25.777 --> 00:20:28.952
or maybe you want to open up
an ice cream shop on Cape Cod.

00:20:28.952 --> 00:20:30.574
Who knows what it may be?

00:20:30.574 --> 00:20:33.565
Maybe you just want to
travel and see the world.

00:20:33.565 --> 00:20:36.494
Maybe you want to go into a relationship

00:20:36.494 --> 00:20:38.087
with someone but you've been afraid to,

00:20:38.087 --> 00:20:41.935
but your heart says it's
the right thing to do.

00:20:41.935 --> 00:20:44.351
All of us feel something,

00:20:44.351 --> 00:20:48.290
and in Leo Tolstoy's famous
novel, The Death of Ivan Ilych,

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:52.457
he asked this question, that
would be terrifying to me.

00:20:53.314 --> 00:20:56.920
He says, as he has his
accountant from Moscow

00:20:56.920 --> 00:20:58.242
lying on his deathbed,

00:20:58.242 --> 00:21:01.374
contemplating the horror of this question:

00:21:01.374 --> 00:21:04.624
"What if my whole life has been wrong?"

00:21:07.412 --> 00:21:09.745
I've known what my music is.

00:21:11.758 --> 00:21:13.675
It's playing right now,

00:21:14.792 --> 00:21:16.024
as I stand here in front of you

00:21:16.024 --> 00:21:18.263
with these cameras and in this place,

00:21:18.263 --> 00:21:20.512
and as I sit down and write my books

00:21:20.512 --> 00:21:24.111
and tell the world what
I know are my truths,

00:21:24.111 --> 00:21:27.983
I feel always completely
on-purpose and fulfilled.

00:21:27.983 --> 00:21:30.421
And no time will I ever
come to the end of my life

00:21:30.421 --> 00:21:33.343
and say, "What if my whole
life has been wrong?"

00:21:33.343 --> 00:21:35.361
Whoever you are, whatever that music is,

00:21:35.361 --> 00:21:37.064
however distant it may sound,

00:21:37.064 --> 00:21:38.894
however strange, however weird

00:21:38.894 --> 00:21:41.398
others may interpret it to be,

00:21:41.398 --> 00:21:44.250
don't get to the end of your life

00:21:44.250 --> 00:21:47.551
and know that you're going to leave

00:21:47.551 --> 00:21:50.295
and not have it played yet.

00:21:50.295 --> 00:21:52.503
Don't die with your music still in you.

00:21:52.503 --> 00:21:53.709
- Thank you so much for watching,

00:21:53.709 --> 00:21:56.327
I made this video because Jason Han,

00:21:56.327 --> 00:21:59.251
video man Jason Han asked me to,

00:21:59.251 --> 00:22:00.601
so if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:22:00.601 --> 00:22:02.365
that you want me to profile next,

00:22:02.365 --> 00:22:04.703
leave it in the comments below

00:22:04.703 --> 00:22:06.009
and I'll see what I can do.

00:22:06.009 --> 00:22:09.320
I'd also love to know which
of Wayne's top ten rules

00:22:09.320 --> 00:22:10.516
meant the most to you,

00:22:10.516 --> 00:22:11.543
leave it in the comments,

00:22:11.543 --> 00:22:12.911
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:22:12.911 --> 00:22:14.105
Thank you so much for watching,

00:22:14.105 --> 00:22:16.681
continue to believe and I'll see you soon.

00:22:16.681 --> 00:22:19.014
(explosion)

